      {
        "id": "s-02",
        "kind": "reading",
        "markdown": "## Why your CSV sanitiser is currently browser-only\n\nRight now, `intake.csv` lives on your machine. You drop it in, the sanitiser validates each row, and you get a clean file back. That entire loop happens inside your browser tab — nothing touches a server.\n\nThat's the correct architecture for what you've described. Adding a backend before you need it would mean hosting a server, keeping it running, and paying for it — all for no benefit yet.\n\nThe question isn't \"should I have a backend?\" It's \"**when** will I hit the wall that forces me to add one?\""
      },
