        "id": "s-03",
        "kind": "callout",
        "tone": "jargon",
        "markdown": "**Backend** — a program running on a computer you don't sit in front of (a data centre machine). For your CSV sanitiser, that would be a program that receives your intake.csv, processes it, and stores the result somewhere both you and a colleague could reach."
      },
      {
        "id": "s-04",
        "kind": "callout",
        "tone": "tip",
        "markdown": "The two walls that force a backend: **sharing** (someone else must see the same data) and **permanence** (the work must survive closing the browser). Your sanitiser currently hits neither wall."
