        "id": "s-05",
        "kind": "code_block",
        "language": "typescript",
        "code": "// Browser-only: intake.csv is read locally, cleaned in memory, downloaded.\n// No server involved.\nasync function sanitiseFile(file: File): Promise<Blob> {\n  const text = await file.text();\n  const rows = parseCSV(text);\n  const cleaned = rows.map(validateRow);\n  return new Blob([toCSV(cleaned)], { type: \"text/csv\" });\n}",
        "explanation": "This is the shape of your current sanitiser — it reads the file, processes it, and produces a download. The whole thing runs in the browser. There is no `fetch` call, no server URL, no storage. That's fine, and correct, for what you're building now."
      },
