              "correct": false,
              "feedback": "Close, but permanence is about the data surviving time (e.g. it must still be there tomorrow). Sharing is the more immediate need here — multiple people accessing the same result."
            },
            {
              "text": "The sharing wall — more than one person needs to see the same data.",
              "correct": true,
              "feedback": "Exactly. Once a second person needs to see the same cleaned output, it can't live only in your browser. That's the sharing wall, and it's when a backend earns its place."
